# Title: Maintenance Escalation
# Summary: A scalable operations benchmark where issue signals move through repeated review and repair stages.
# Benchmark Family: maintenance_escalation
# Repair_1: Operators coordinate a repair action at maintenance stage 1.
# Repair_2: Operators coordinate a repair action at maintenance stage 2.
# Repair_3: Operators coordinate a repair action at maintenance stage 3.
# Review_1: Operators review the signal at maintenance stage 1.
# Review_2: Operators review the signal at maintenance stage 2.
# Review_3: Operators review the signal at maintenance stage 3.
# Signal_1: An issue signal is detected at maintenance stage 1.
# Signal_2: An issue signal is detected at maintenance stage 2.
# Signal_3: An issue signal is detected at maintenance stage 3.

prior_1: 0.122 <= P(Repair_1) <= 0.295
prior_2: 0.076 <= P(Repair_2) <= 0.302
prior_3: 0.0 <= P(Repair_3) <= 0.203
prior_4: 0.168 <= P(Review_1) <= 0.372
prior_5: 0.249 <= P(Review_2) <= 0.345
prior_6: 0.212 <= P(Review_3) <= 0.39
prior_7: 0.012 <= P(Signal_1) <= 0.227
prior_8: 0.104 <= P(Signal_2) <= 0.294
prior_9: 0.011 <= P(Signal_3) <= 0.194
component_1: 0.122 <= P(Repair_1 and Review_1) <= 0.23
component_2: 0.076 <= P(Repair_2 and Review_2) <= 0.27
component_3: 0.0 <= P(Repair_3 and Review_3) <= 0.203
link_1: 0.211 <= P(Repair_1 and Review_1 | Signal_1) <= 0.417
link_2: 0.583 <= P(Signal_2 | Repair_1 and Review_1) <= 0.71
link_3: 0.228 <= P(Repair_2 and Review_2 | Signal_2) <= 0.42
link_4: 0.459 <= P(Signal_3 | Repair_2 and Review_2) <= 0.579
link_5: 0.317 <= P(Repair_3 and Review_3 | Signal_3) <= 0.439
